                <pb facs="0163" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg141"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The first meeting of the NAT Council Deputies was
                    held on July 25. Spofford was unanimously elected permanent Chairman. The
                    Deputies decided to meet daily at 3 p. m. and to prepare daily summaries of
                    decisions rather than keep verbatim records. They tentatively agreed to limit
                    communications to the press to official council statements. This information was
                    transmitted from London in telegram 549, Depto
                    6, of July 25 (not printed, 740.5/7–2550). Thereafter, most telegrams sent from
                    London by Spofford carried a Depto number
                    only.</p>
                <p>Much of the detailed coverage of the Council Deputies’ meetings, not included in
                    this compilation, is in Department of State file 740.5.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
